    <!-- First-run guide -->
    <string name="guide_title">Getting crags in</string>
    <string name="guide_body">1. Tap Add crags. UKC’s own crag search opens inside the app.

2. Type a place or postcode into the location box, choose a distance, and search. That is all — there is no need to open or pick crags one at a time.

3. Tap Import all at the bottom of the results. Every crag the search found is queued and read in the background while the app is open; the line at the top of your crag list counts down what is left.

4. Optional: sign in to UKC under My logbook, then Sync my logbook to bring your ticks, wishlist and ticklists across.

Topos are saved with every crag. To keep photos for somewhere with no signal, open a crag and choose Save photos offline from its menu.

This guide is in Settings if you want it again.</string>
